<p>Morgan's Point Resort is a residential community on the shore of Lake Belton, west of Temple and northwest of Belton. Its setting on the water is the main draw, and the homes there include full-time residences as well as lake houses that sit empty for stretches of time. From our base in Temple, it is a short drive out to the lake.</p>

<h2>Why Lakeside Roofs Need Extra Attention</h2>
<p>Open water gives wind a long, unbroken run before it reaches the shoreline. When a storm moves across Lake Belton, homes facing the lake can take stronger, more direct gusts than homes a few streets back. Over time that shows up on the roof in specific ways:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Lifted and creased shingles</strong> along the edges, rakes and ridges that face the water</li>
<li><strong>Broken shingle seal strips</strong>, which let wind-driven rain work under the shingles</li>
<li><strong>Loose ridge caps and vents</strong> that rattle loose a little more with each storm</li>
<li><strong>Damaged drip edge and fascia</strong> where wind gets under the roof edge</li>
</ul>
<p>Wind damage is not always dramatic. A few lifted shingles can go unnoticed until the next heavy rain finds the gap. Our <a href="/services/wind-damage-roof-repair-temple-tx/">wind damage roof repair</a> service focuses on finding and securing those weak spots before they leak.</p>

<h2>Housing in Morgan's Point Resort</h2>
<p>The community has a mix of older lake homes, mid-sized family houses and newer construction. Many lots are wooded, and some sit on sloped ground that falls toward the water. Older homes may have had additions, decks or screened porches added over the years, each creating another roof joint to flash. Trees bring their own issues: falling limbs during storms, leaves packed into valleys and gutters, and shaded areas that stay damp longer.</p>
<p>For part-time residents, a small leak can run for weeks before anyone notices. If you are away often, a periodic inspection is cheap insurance against interior damage. Our article on <a href="/blog/how-often-roof-inspection-temple-tx/">how often to inspect your roof</a> offers a sensible schedule.</p>

<!--cta-->

<h2>Storms, Hail and Heat at the Lake</h2>
<p>Lake Belton homes face the same Central Texas weather as the rest of Bell County: spring and fall severe storms with hail, summer heat and strong UV, and occasional winter freezes. The added wind exposure makes good installation especially important. When we replace a roof here, we pay close attention to nailing, starter strips at the edges, ridge cap attachment and sealing at roof penetrations, since those details decide how well a roof handles high wind.</p>

